function CareerLab({notify}){const [role,setRole]=useState('Data Analyst'),[answer,setAnswer]=useState(''),[result,setResult]=useState(null),[loading,setLoading]=useState(false);const submit=async()=>{setLoading(true);try{const d=await api('/innovation/career-lab',{method:'POST',body:JSON.stringify({role,answer})});setResult(d);notify('Career experiment evaluated')}catch(e){notify(e.message,'err')}finally{setLoading(false)}};return <><Title eyebrow="TRY BEFORE YOU CHOOSE" title="Career Experiment Lab" sub="Test the kind of thinking the role requires, then get AI feedback."/><div className="panel"><div className="filters"><select value={role} onChange={e=>setRole(e.target.value)}><option>Data Analyst</option><option>Software Developer</option><option>Product Manager</option><option>UX Designer</option></select></div><h3>Mini challenge</h3><p>A retail team sees weekend sales rise 35% while returns also rise. What would you investigate first, and why?</p><textarea value={answer} onChange={e=>setAnswer(e.target.value)} placeholder="Explain your first step and reasoning…"/><Button className="primary" onClick={submit} loading={loading}>Evaluate experiment <I.Sparkles/></Button>{result&&<div className="quizResult"><div className="scoreCircle">{result.score}</div><div><h3>Career Fit Signal: {result.score}%</h3><p>{result.feedback}</p><b>Next challenge:</b> {result.next_challenge}</div></div>}</div></>}

